\section{Constraint Algebra and Closure}

The constraints obey
\begin{equation}
  \{\mathcal{G}^a(x), \mathcal{G}^b(y)\}
  =
  f^{abc}\mathcal{G}^c(x)\delta^{(3)}(x-y),
\end{equation}
\begin{equation}
  \{\mathcal{H}_i(x), \mathcal{H}_j(y)\}
  =
  \mathcal{H}_j(x)\partial_i\delta^{(3)}(x-y)
  -
  \mathcal{H}_i(y)\partial_j\delta^{(3)}(x-y),
\end{equation}
and
\begin{equation}
  \{\mathcal{H}(x), \mathcal{H}(y)\}
  =
  \gamma^{ij}(x)\mathcal{H}_j(x)\partial_i\delta^{(3)}(x-y)
  -
  \gamma^{ij}(y)\mathcal{H}_j(y)\partial_i\delta^{(3)}(y-x)
  +
  \Omega(x,y),
\end{equation}
with $\Omega(x,y)\to 0$ under the CKKS noise-damping condition and $\ell_P\to 0$, yielding the standard hypersurface deformation algebra. Thus the system is first-class and consistent.

\section{BRST Charge and Physical Hilbert Space}

We extend the phase space with ghosts $(c^a,\xi^i,\omega)$ and anti-ghosts. The total BRST charge is
\begin{equation}
  \mathbf{Q}_{\text{BRST}}
  =
  \int d^3x\,
  \Big[
    c^a \mathcal{G}^a
    +
    \xi^i \mathcal{H}_i
    +
    \omega \mathcal{H}_{\text{CKKS}}
    + \dots
